# Round 10 (2026-09-10): `! Access-Control-Allow-Origin` detaches the `*` that Cloudflare Pages adds to every asset by
# default (seen on the bare pages.dev origin too — not a zone rule, not ours). COOP/CORP mirror the app. The
# Content-Security-Policy line is a PLACEHOLDER: scripts/mkt_csp_headers.mjs (gate 3 of scripts/mkt_deploy.sh) replaces
# it in dist/_headers with the enforced policy + the SHA-256 of every inline script in the build. A deploy that skips
# the gate ships the literal placeholder, which browsers ignore as an unknown directive (nothing breaks, nothing is
# enforced) — the gate is what makes the header real.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: __MKT_CSP__
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
